Ladybird now runs an assignment to a class declaration’s binding that
reads the binding (“C = C”, “C += 1”) without a ReferenceError, and
still throws for one that runs before the declaration. V8, JSC, and
SpiderMonkey give the same results for all three cases, as the spec
requires: Evaluating a ClassDeclaration initializes its binding with
InitializeBoundName before any code after the declaration runs.
